{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1138431-wanting-to-make-custom-character-sheets","id":1138431,"title":"Wanting to make custom (character) sheets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-07T16:06:01-07:00","id":1138431,"title":"Wanting to make custom (character) sheets","content":"So, as the title states, I'm interested in making custom character sheets for the Chronicles of Darkness games I am in (or perhaps other games, we'll see). Naturally, the good Mr Gone has made plenty of very useful and practical sheets. It's just that, after hearing about other people making personalized sheets for their games, I'm kind of wondering what it'd be like if I were to throw my hat into that practice. Make something for my character that is very...them.<br /> <br /> However, the problem is that I'm not sure where to start there. I had thought of using Print Shop, but a friend recommended that I use a PDF program in order to make sure it is interactive once done. Does anyone have any recommendations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T17:07:23-07:00","id":1138455,"title":"","content":"Hey!! That's awesome you're thinking about trying to make your own character sheets!!<br /> <br /> As for recommendations...well, I use a full version of Adobe Acrobat. It's an oooold version(Version 5), but it's works pretty good for me. The newer ones have some quirks that have kept from me using them, but they might work well for you. I hear Adobe InDesign might be good to use as well. Or, you could always use Word or something along those lines and then convert to PDF at the end.<br /> <br /> Not sure that helps...but maybe it'll give you a few ideas on where to start. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T18:12:11-07:00","id":1138469,"title":"","content":"I like to start with InDesign or Illustrator these days, though if I add form filling or interactivity to the sheet I usually do that in a full version of Adobe Acrobat - not sure I can't do it in InDesign, just familiar with the how-to in Acrobat so I haven't bothered to find any new ways to do it.<br /> <br /> Really, my suggestion boils down to this: try whatever you can get your hands on, and see what works best for you. Years ago when I first internet-met Mr. Gone I was using MS Paint to make my character sheets, and I think he was already using the version of Adobe Acrobat he still uses now back then, so I tried it out and it was completely unfathomable to me that it was even possible to make character sheets with the program because it and I just didn't &quot;gel&quot;... but then I got the idea to try out some other programs that came with the Creative Suite I got Acrobat as part of, and found that InDesign was completely intuitive to me and worked great (and later started incorporating Illustrator just to have a bit flashier graphics on the sheets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T00:04:21-07:00","id":1138521,"title":"","content":"Wow. I honestly didn't expect to get advice so quickly, much less from people who are so experienced. Thank you for sharing your experiences, as well as what you use for your own projects.<br /> <br /> The only problem I see with Adobe (or InDesign at least) is that it appears to be a monthly subscription service, which I'm...hesitant about. While I can pay for it, and it's hardly going to put me into debt doing so, I have problems with starting something and then simply petering out before I can really do anything with it. Having a subscription service on something that may take me far longer than it needs to, and something I'd not have a great number of uses outside of gaming for, is...well, as noted, something I'm hesitant over. Still, you do pay for quality, so I should at least give the trials a good run through their paces.<br /> <br /> One alternative I have is Foxit Reader; I've been using it for my PDF reading needs for a while, since Adobe Reader had an annoying habit of freezing and crashing when I used it. I've just found that it has a PDF creator and editor option one can purchase. More expensive in the short-term, but it is a single purchase. I'm sure I'll find other options, given a bit of time.<br /> <br /> Again, thank you Mr Gone, Drake, for giving me a jumping off point. I may not be starting immediately, but I definitely have something to start <i>from</i>.<br /> <br /> Have a great night. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T04:28:20-07:00","id":1138546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1138431-wanting-to-make-custom-character-sheets?p=1138469#post1138469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Years ago when I first internet-met Mr. Gone I was using MS Paint to make my character sheets, and I think he was already using the version of Adobe Acrobat he still uses now back then, so I tried it out and it was completely unfathomable to me that it was even possible to make character sheets with the program because it and I just didn't &quot;gel&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm still using the same version of Acrobat...it's going on like 15 years now. lol. I've been using it so long, I'm almost afraid to switch to anything else.<br /> <br /> And I will fully admit, it's crazy the way I use it too. I'm sure it was never intended to be used the way I'm using it(which is probably why it crashes sometimes). I'm not even sure why I started using it that way..lol. But, it seems to work for me. I probably should try something else one of these days..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1138431-wanting-to-make-custom-character-sheets?p=1138521#post1138521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One alternative I have is Foxit Reader; I've been using it for my PDF reading needs for a while, since Adobe Reader had an annoying habit of freezing and crashing when I used it. I've just found that it has a PDF creator and editor option one can purchase. More expensive in the short-term, but it is a single purchase. I'm sure I'll find other options, given a bit of time.<br /> <br /> Again, thank you Mr Gone, Drake, for giving me a jumping off point. I may not be starting immediately, but I definitely have something to start <i>from</i>.<br /> <br /> Have a great night. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're very welcome! Glad we could help a bit.<br /> <br /> I thought about suggesting Foxit, as I knew they had a pdf editor and then I completely spaced on it. Glad you knew about it though. Hope it works well for you!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}